# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OSI — the single environment file for the whole project (root only).
# Committed on purpose: keep it SECRET-FREE. Put local secrets in .env.local
# (gitignored). Both compose files load this file via `env_file: - .env`.
#
# NODE_ENV and the host port are intentionally NOT set here:
#   - NODE_ENV is set per environment by the tooling / compose (dev vs prod).
#     Pinning it here breaks production builds (dev JSX runtime leaks in).
#   - The exposed host port default is 3010 everywhere (dev AND prod — same port);
#     override per run with `WEB_PORT=<port> docker compose ...` if needed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database (engine TBD — see src/database). Uncomment and fill in once chosen.
# Real credentials go in .env.local, never here.
# DB_PORT=5432
# POSTGRES_USER=osi
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DB=osi
# DATABASE_URL=
